I have enough to answer. The fault is geo's crash-looping pod; search and frontend inherit it. I'll write up the result.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "geo",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_k8s_pod_name, min(value) AS min_restarts, max(value) AS max_restarts, count(*) AS samples FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name = 'geo-85ff5d94fc-5njsl' AND metric = 'k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Geo pod container restart counter climbs from 3 to 6 during the abnormal window, repeatedly restarting."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'abn' AS p, count(*) AS geo_spans FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'geo' UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name = 'geo'", "claim": "Geo emits about 1161 server spans in normal period and essentially none in the abnormal period."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT attr_status_code, count(*) AS n, approx_quantile(duration, 0.5)/1e6 AS p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'search' AND span_name = 'geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Search's calls to geo.Geo/Nearby mostly return Error within about 0.02 ms, i.e. fast refused connections."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "geo", "to": "search", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT attr_status_code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'search' AND span_name = 'search.Search/Nearby' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Search's Nearby server spans turn to Error (1133 of about 1137) when its geo calls fail."}]},
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code, count(*) AS n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name = 'frontend' AND span_name = 'HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Frontend HTTP /hotels requests fail with Error status (1099) while other frontend routes stay Unset."}]}
  ]
}
```

